Absolutely! I'll give you two examples: one for an advertisement and one for a regular website element. Both are healthcare-specific. Let's start with an ad example.

### Advertisement Example:
```html
<div class="ad-banner" id="ad-slot-health-300x250" data-ad-id="healthcare-ad-001" data-campaign="wellness-promo">
 <style>
 .ad-banner { 
 width: 300px; 
 height: 250px; 
 border: 1px solid #c0c0c0; 
 box-shadow: 0 0 5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
 }
 .ad-content {
 display: flex;
 justify-content: center;
 align-items: center;
 background-color: #fff;
 }
 .cta-button {
 color: #1a73e8;
 text-decoration: none;
 font-weight: bold;
 }
 </style>
 <div class="ad-content">
 <img src="health-banner.jpg" alt="Wellness Savings">
 <a href="#" class="cta-button">Learn More</a>
 </div>
 <script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js"></script>
 <ins class="adsbygoogle" data-ad-client="ca-pub-1234567890"></ins>
</div>
```
Classification: is_ad: true
Ad Type: banner

### Non-Advertisement Example:
```html
<nav class="site-navigation">
 <ul class="nav-menu">
 <li><a href="/health-news">Health News</a></li>
 <li><a href="/services">Our Services</a></li>
 <li><a href="/contact-us">Contact Us</a></li>
 </ul>
 <style>
 .site-navigation {
 background-color: #f8f9fa;
 padding: 10px;
 border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
 }
 .nav-menu li {
 display: inline;
 margin-right: 15px;
 }
 .nav-menu a {
 color: #333;
 text-decoration: none;
 }
 </style>
</nav>
```
Classification: is_ad: false

These examples use common patterns found on healthcare websites. The ad example incorporates typical ad network code elements, while the non-ad example uses navigation structures without promotional content.

Sure, let's start with an example of an advertisement commonly found on healthcare websites, such as an ad for prescription drugs or medical services.

Here's a snippet of HTML code with the accompanying CSS and JavaScript for an ad banner example:

```html
<div class="ad-banner" id="healthcare-ad-slot" data-ad-id="56789" data-campaign="health-boost-campaign">
 <style>
 .ad-banner {
 width: 320px;
 height: 50px;
 border: 1px solid #ccc;
 margin: 10px 0;
 background-color: #f9f9f9;
 text-align: center;
 position: relative;
 }
 .ad-banner img {
 max-width: 100%;
 height: auto;
 }
 .cta-button {
 display: inline-block;
 margin-top: 5px;
 padding: 8px 15px;
 background-color: #2b7a78;
 color: #fff;
 text-decoration: none;
 font-weight: bold;
 border-radius: 4px;
 }
 </style>
 <div class="ad-content">
 <img src="health-product.jpg" alt="Promote Your Health">
 <a href="#" class="cta-button">Discover More</a>
 </div>
 <script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js"></script>
 <ins class="adsbygoogle"
 style="display:block"
 data-ad-client="ca-pub-9876543210"
 data-ad-slot="1234567890"
 data-ad-format="auto"
 data-full-width-responsive="true"></ins>
 <script>
 (adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});
 </script>
</div>
```
Classification: is_ad: true 
Ad Type: banner

This HTML snippet represents a realistic ad banner that could be seen on a healthcare website. It includes typical elements such as inline styles defining the ad's visual appearance, an image promoting a health product, and a "Discover More" call-to-action button. It also integrates common ad network codes from Google AdSense.

Of course! Here's a typical non-advertisement example composed of a basic article section that you might find on a healthcare website:

```html
<article class="health-article">
 <style>
 .health-article {
 background-color: #ffffff;
 padding: 20px;
 margin: 20px 0;
 border: 1px solid #ddd;
 border-radius: 5px;
 }
 .article-title {
 font-size: 1.5rem;
 font-weight: bold;
 color: #333;
 }
 .article-content p {
 line-height: 1.6;
 color: #555;
 margin: 10px 0;
 }
 </style>
 <h1 class="article-title">Understanding the Importance of Regular Health Check-Ups</h1>
 <div class="article-content">
 <p>Regular health check-ups can help detect potential health issues before they become serious. By monitoring your health regularly, you can take preventative measures and maintain a healthy lifestyle.</p>
 <p>Consult your healthcare provider to determine how often you should have check-ups based on your age, gender, and medical history.</p>
 </div>
</article>
```
Classification: is_ad: false

This HTML snippet provides a glimpse into a simple article component commonly found on healthcare websites. It includes text content intended for informational purposes and lacks any ad-related identifiers or scripts. The CSS styles provide a clean presentation, enhancing the article's readability.
